.TH CSTR_CONSTRUCT 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Macros"
.SH NAME
cstr_construct \- declare and initialise a cstr in one step
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <cstring.h>

cstr_construct(s, initial);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Combines cstr_declare() and cstr_init() into a single statement. Creates a
new cstr variable named s and initialises it with the given content.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
s        Variable name to create
initial  Initial content (C string or NULL for empty string)
.fi
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
cstr_construct(greeting, "Hello");
cstr_append(greeting, ", world!");
cstr_destroy(greeting);
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR cstr_construct_scoped (3),
.BR cstr_construct_mp (3),
.BR cstr_declare (3),
.BR cstr_init (3)
